# XSH fpathconf(), pathconf()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# The tests query only the names of the DESCRIPTION table that <unistd.h>
# defines; a missing name is noted (a header matter, XBD <unistd.h>).
# Which file types a name must be supported for follows the Requirements
# notes of the table: where a note leaves the association unspecified
# for a file type, the tests do not query that name on that type. Names
# whose variable depends on an option the system does not support
# (RETURN VALUE: unspecified) are skipped: the {POSIX_*_XFER_*} and
# {POSIX_ALLOC_SIZE_MIN} variables and _PC_FALLOC need ADV, _PC_PRIO_IO
# needs PIO, _PC_SYNC_IO needs SIO.
#
# Results describe the file system of the test's working directory.

assertion  XSH.fpathconf.001
anchor     functions/fpathconf.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/fpathconf.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      1988
says       For a directory, pathconf() and fpathconf() of every name whose
           association with directories the Requirements notes do not
           leave unspecified ({FILESIZEBITS}, {LINK_MAX}, {NAME_MAX},
           {PATH_MAX}, {PIPE_BUF}, {POSIX2_SYMLINKS}, {SYMLINK_MAX},
           {TEXTDOMAIN_MAX}, _POSIX_CHOWN_RESTRICTED, _POSIX_NO_TRUNC,
           _POSIX_TIMESTAMP_RESOLUTION) return a value or -1, and leave
           errno unchanged either way (never -1 with errno set).
test       t/001-directory.c

assertion  XSH.fpathconf.002
anchor     functions/fpathconf.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/fpathconf.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      1988
says       For a regular file, pathconf() and fpathconf() of {LINK_MAX},
           _POSIX_CHOWN_RESTRICTED, _POSIX_TIMESTAMP_RESOLUTION,
           _POSIX_ASYNC_IO, and (with the options they need) _POSIX_FALLOC,
           _POSIX_PRIO_IO, _POSIX_SYNC_IO and the five ADV transfer
           variables return a value or -1, and leave errno unchanged
           either way (never -1 with errno set).
note       The Requirements notes of these names leave no association
           with regular files unspecified; the may-fail [EINVAL] for an
           unsupported association is read as applying only where a note
           leaves the association unspecified.
test       t/002-regular-file.c

assertion  XSH.fpathconf.003
anchor     functions/fpathconf.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     basedefs/limits.h.html#Pathname Variable Values
class      required
since      1988
says       fpathconf() of _PC_PIPE_BUF on both ends of a pipe and on a
           FIFO opened for reading, and pathconf() of it on the FIFO's
           path, return -1 leaving errno unchanged (no limit) or at least
           {_POSIX_PIPE_BUF} (512).
test       t/003-pipe-buf.c

assertion  XSH.fpathconf.004
anchor     basedefs/limits.h.html#Pathname Variable Values
anchor     basedefs/limits.h.html#Minimum Values
anchor     functions/fpathconf.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      1988
says       For a directory, pathconf() returns -1 leaving errno unchanged
           (no limit) or at least the minimum acceptable value:
           {FILESIZEBITS} 32, {LINK_MAX} 8, {NAME_MAX} 14 (255 on XSI
           systems), {PATH_MAX} 256 (1024 on XSI systems), {PIPE_BUF} 512,
           {SYMLINK_MAX} 255, {TEXTDOMAIN_MAX} 11 (252 on XSI systems).
test       t/004-minimum-values.c

assertion  XSH.fpathconf.005
anchor     functions/fpathconf.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     basedefs/limits.h.html#Pathname Variable Values
anchor     basedefs/unistd.h.html#Execution-Time Symbolic Constants
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap02.html#2.1.6
class      required
since      2001
says       The values agree with the headers: each pathname limit that
           <limits.h> defines is matched on a directory by -1 (no limit)
           or at least the header's value; _POSIX_NO_TRUNC and
           _POSIX_CHOWN_RESTRICTED defined greater than zero are matched
           on a directory by a value other than -1;
           _POSIX_TIMESTAMP_RESOLUTION and _POSIX2_SYMLINKS, where
           defined, are the values for a directory and (resolution) a
           regular file; _POSIX_ASYNC_IO, _POSIX_PRIO_IO, _POSIX_SYNC_IO
           and _POSIX_FALLOC defined as -1 are matched by -1 on a regular
           file, and defined otherwise by a value other than -1.
test       t/005-header-consistency.c

assertion  XSH.fpathconf.006
anchor     functions/fpathconf.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap04.html#4.12
class      required
since      2008
says       pathconf() of _PC_TIMESTAMP_RESOLUTION on a directory and on a
           regular file returns a value from 1 to 1000000000: a
           resolution in nanoseconds no coarser than one second.
note       UNRESOLVED where <unistd.h> lacks _PC_TIMESTAMP_RESOLUTION.
test       t/006-timestamp-resolution.c

assertion  XSH.fpathconf.007
anchor     functions/fpathconf.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     basedefs/limits.h.html#Pathname Variable Values
class      required
since      1988
says       On the controlling terminal (opened by the name ctermid()
           gives), fpathconf() of _PC_MAX_CANON and _PC_MAX_INPUT returns -1
           leaving errno unchanged or at least 255, and of _PC_VDISABLE a
           value or -1 leaving errno unchanged; never -1 with errno set.
note       UNRESOLVED when the process has no controlling terminal (as
           under the harness); XSH.fpathconf.012 checks the same on a
           pseudo-terminal where XSI provides one.
test       t/007-terminal.c

assertion  XSH.fpathconf.008
anchor     functions/fpathconf.html#ERRORS/EINVAL
anchor     functions/fpathconf.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      1988
says       pathconf(".", -1), pathconf(".", 0x7ffffff0), and fpathconf()
           with the same names on an open directory, return -1 with errno
           EINVAL.
note       Implementations may define further names; the test checks that
           no name of the table has these values.
test       t/008-invalid-name.c

assertion  XSH.fpathconf.009
anchor     functions/fpathconf.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     functions/fpathconf.html#ERRORS/ENOENT
class      required
since      2001
says       pathconf() of every name of the table on a path that does not
           exist returns a value leaving errno unchanged, or -1 leaving
           errno unchanged, or -1 with errno ENOENT or EINVAL; never -1
           with another errno.
note       No name is required to depend on the file (<limits.h>
           Pathname Variable Values), so an implementation need not look
           at the path (RATIONALE); [ENOENT] and [EINVAL] are may-fail.
test       t/009-missing-path.c

assertion  XSH.fpathconf.010
anchor     functions/fpathconf.html#RETURN VALUE
anchor     functions/fpathconf.html#ERRORS/EBADF
class      required
since      2001
says       fpathconf() of every name of the table on a descriptor that is
           not open returns a value leaving errno unchanged, or -1 leaving
           errno unchanged, or -1 with errno EBADF or EINVAL; never -1
           with another errno.
note       As for XSH.fpathconf.009: the implementation need not look at
           the descriptor; [EBADF] and [EINVAL] are may-fail.
test       t/010-bad-descriptor.c

assertion  XSH.fpathconf.011
anchor     functions/fpathconf.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     basedefs/limits.h.html#Pathname Variable Values
anchor     basedefs/unistd.h.html#Constants for Options and Option Groups
class      required
since      1988
says       With n = pathconf(".", _PC_NAME_MAX) (not -1, below 4096): a
           file whose name has n bytes (portable filename characters) can
           be created in the directory; and where pathconf(".",
           _PC_NO_TRUNC) is not -1, creating one whose name has n + 1
           bytes fails with ENAMETOOLONG.
test       t/011-name-max-applies.c

assertion  XSH.fpathconf.012
anchor     functions/fpathconf.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     basedefs/limits.h.html#Pathname Variable Values
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1988
says       On a pseudo-terminal's slave side (posix_openpt()),
           fpathconf() of _PC_MAX_CANON and _PC_MAX_INPUT returns -1
           leaving errno unchanged or at least 255, and of _PC_VDISABLE a
           value or -1 leaving errno unchanged; never -1 with errno set.
note       The requirement is Base (XSH.fpathconf.007); only this setup,
           posix_openpt(), needs XSI.
test       t/012-pty-terminal.c
